Observe the supplied clip and report what happens in it.

The clip covers {{ start_ms }}..{{ end_ms }} ms of the recording. Report every
timestamp in that range, measured from the start of the recording rather than
from the start of the clip.

Rules:
- Report only what the clip shows or says. Do not infer events it does not cover.
- Report at most {{ max_events }} events, keeping the most consequential ones.
- Separate readable on-screen text from visual interpretation in the wording.
- Give each event the narrowest range that contains it.
- State uncertainty in the event text when a detail cannot be made out.

Return one JSON object with an `events` array. Each event has:
`start_ms`, `end_ms`, `text`, and `entities` (array of names read or recognized).
